{
  "id": "kukhnya-s06e19-scene-04",
  "pair": "ru-en",
  "title": "Предложение сбежать вдвоём  (An Offer to Run Away Together)",
  "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
  "voices": {
    "narrator": "sky",
    "anya": "alisa",
    "denis": "anja"
  },
  "labels": {
    "anya": "Катя",
    "denis": "Денис"
  },
  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Denis uses a key from reception to enter Katya's room while she is still in her wedding dress. He apologizes for his harsh words the day before and begs her to run away with him to Paris, Milan, or Voronezh while there is still time.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Денис, как ты сюда попал?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "denis",
      "t": "Я хотел с тобой поговорить.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "До свадьбы нельзя меня видеть.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "denis",
      "t": "Мне можно, я не жених.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "denis",
      "t": "Я пришёл попросить у тебя прощения.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я на тебя не обижаюсь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Это всё уже в прошлом.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "denis",
      "t": "Давай сегодня уедем отсюда вдвоём.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "denis",
      "t": "Мы начнём нашу жизнь сначала.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "И куда же мы поедем?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "denis",
      "t": "Да куда угодно, выбирай сама.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "denis",
      "t": "Поверь, сейчас ещё не поздно.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Денис, как ты сюда попал?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Denis, how did you get in here?' Katya raises the pitch on 'got in' to turn the phrase into a direct spoken question.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "denis",
      "t": "Я хотел с тобой поговорить.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I wanted to talk with you.' Denis anchors the line on 'I', while 'to talk' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "До свадьбы нельзя меня видеть.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Before the wedding you must not see me.' The grammar packs 'until' and 'to see' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange. Denis answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "denis",
      "t": "Мне можно, я не жених.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am allowed, I am not the groom.' The meaning hinges on 'to me' working together with 'groom' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "denis",
      "t": "Я пришёл попросить у тебя прощения.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I came to ask your forgiveness.' The '-l' ending on the verb meaning 'arrived' places the action in the masculine past tense.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я на тебя не обижаюсь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am not angry with you.' Notice how Russian expresses 'I' and 'am offended' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Это всё уже в прошлом.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'All of that is already in the past.' Notice how Russian expresses 'this' and 'last' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "denis",
      "t": "Давай сегодня уедем отсюда вдвоём.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Let us leave here together today.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'come on' before landing on 'the two of us'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "denis",
      "t": "Мы начнём нашу жизнь сначала.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We will start our life over.' Denis brings out the contrast between 'we' and 'let us begin' in a few short words. Katya answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "И куда же мы поедем?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And where will we go?' Katya brings out the contrast between 'and' and 'where to' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "denis",
      "t": "Да куда угодно, выбирай сама.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Anywhere at all, choose for yourself.' The grammar packs 'yes' and 'myself' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "denis",
      "t": "Поверь, сейчас ещё не поздно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Believe me, right now it is not too late.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'believe' and finishing on 'late'. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Денис, как ты сюда попал?",
      "gap": 0.5
